    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30906" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nīcŏmēdes</span></b> ,
		is, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νικομήδης</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Son of Prusias, a king of Bithynia</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. de
				Or. 2, 61, 229</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Verr. 2, 1, 24, §
			63</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The son of the former, who declared himself a
				freedman of the Roman people</i>, <i><span class="en">Just. 34,
			4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">38, 5</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Suet. Caes. 2</span></i>.</div>
